# Component Development Patterns

## Component Organization
- Place all components in [src/components/](mdc:src/components/) directory
- Use PascalCase for component file names
- Create separate files for each component
- Group related components in subdirectories when needed

## Component Structure
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  // Define all props with proper types
}

export const ComponentName = ({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentProps) => {
  // Hooks at the top
  // Event handlers
  // Render logic
  return (
    // JSX
  );
};
```

## UI Component Usage
- Use components from [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/) for consistent design
- Import with proper version aliases (e.g., `@radix-ui/react-button@1.1.2`)
- Customize UI components with Tailwind classes
- Use the `cn()` utility for conditional class names

## State Management in Components
- Use local state for component-specific data
- Lift state up to parent components when shared
- Use proper TypeScript types for state variables
- Implement proper state updates with functional updates when needed

## Event Handling
- Define event handlers as arrow functions
- Use proper TypeScript event types
- Implement proper error handling in event handlers
- Use callback props for parent communication

## Accessibility
- Use proper ARIA attributes
- Implement keyboard navigation
- Ensure proper focus management
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide proper alt text for images

## Persian/Farsi Content
- All user-facing text must be in Persian
- Use proper RTL layout with `dir="rtl"`
- Test text rendering with Vazirmatn font
- Ensure proper text alignment and spacing